# Code Quality

- Match existing style. Introduce no ESLint or TypeScript errors (`npm run lint` runs `tsc` plus ESLint with `--max-warnings 0`).
- Prefer functional components, existing utilities (for example `insertIf`), and GOV.UK class names over custom CSS.
- Reduce and simplify: avoid duplication, remove dead code, and keep components and utilities minimal.

When generating code, prioritize correct TypeScript types, testable components, and small diffs. Do not skip tests or Storybook for new or changed UI.
